## AI Coding Assistant Rules File

This file defines all project rules, coding standards, workflow guidelines, references, documentation structures, and best practices.  It is a living document and will evolve over time.

## PROJECT DOCUMENTATION & CONTEXT SYSTEM

* All components should have entrance and exit animations defined.  Mobile menu items should have matching entrance and exit animations.  (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* All animations should mirror entrance animations where appropriate. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* Mobile layout and UI should be optimized for the `@features-section.tsx` component.  Specific improvements include: stacked vertical layout for features on mobile; logical feature order with clean borders and spacing;  hidden absolute positioning layout on mobile (desktop only); reduced mobile text sizes; responsive margins/padding; darker backgrounds (60% opacity); backdrop blur for legibility; disabled mobile rotation and scaling effects; optimized image quality (90 instead of 100) with `sizes='100vw'`; full-width mobile CTA button;  added left border accent to mobile feature cards. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* Desktop feature tooltips should have purposeful placement, clearly referencing aspects of the lighter in the background image. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* The background image should crossfade between the white and black lighter images. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* A sticky sub-navigation should be implemented below the main navigation, aligned right on desktop, containing email and phone contact buttons.  Mobile version should display these buttons below the main navigation items. (Added 2025-05-15)  Buttons should utilize `lucide-react` icons for email and phone. (Added 2025-05-15)  Desktop buttons should have a semi-transparent black background with backdrop blur and smooth entrance animations. (Added 2025-05-15)  The desktop email button should utilize a dropdown menu to allow the user to select their preferred email client (Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo, or default). (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request) The mobile email button should also utilize a dropdown menu for email client selection. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* The contact sub-navigation should include a dropdown menu for email client selection on both desktop and mobile versions.  (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)  The dropdown should offer options for Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo, and the default email client. (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* Phone number clicks should utilize the `tel:` URL scheme for direct dialing.  (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)  Additionally, a dropdown menu should be provided to allow users to select their preferred calling application (Phone, WhatsApp, Skype, FaceTime, Telegram, SMS). (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)
* Implement an AI chatbot modal UI, modeled after employee Ibrahim, using the Vercel AI SDK UI.  The modal should be accessible from most pages, support desktop and mobile layouts, persist messages, have entrance/exit animations, and be dismissible.  The chatbot should use the `useChat` hook, be styled with shadcn/ui and Tailwind, and have a backend API route (e.g., `/api/chat`). (Added 2025-05-15 based on user request)  The chatbot should display Ibrahim’s avatar and name in the header. The chat UI should use the Vercel AI SDK’s `useChat` hook for real-time streaming. The modal should be styled with shadcn/ui and Tailwind, matching the site’s design system. The chatbot should have a friendly, helpful, and knowledgeable tone, reflecting Ibrahim’s persona. The modal should not interfere with other UI elements (z-index, focus management). The modal should be accessible (ARIA roles, keyboard navigation). The chatbot should handle errors gracefully (e.g., API errors, network issues). The modal should be responsive and mobile-optimized.  The chatbot should use a backend API route (e.g., `/api/chat`) for model interaction. The modal should not require authentication for basic use. The chatbot should not expose sensitive company information. The modal should be performant and not bloat the initial page load (dynamic import). The chatbot should have a recognizable icon/button for opening (e.g., chat bubble with Ibrahim’s avatar).
